# Settings for one homelab-helios installation. Copy to .env and restrict it (cp .env.example .env &&
# chmod 600 .env); .env is gitignored and never committed. Every setting the stack reads is listed here and in
# docs/interfaces.md.
#
# No secrets belong in this file. Each service keeps its own logins, tokens and keys in its data directory. Plex's
# one-time claim token, the only secret a service takes from its environment, goes in a gitignored plex.env.

# On a host with an NVIDIA GPU (and the NVIDIA Container Toolkit), add compose.gpu.yaml so Plex transcodes on it;
# with an Intel GPU, compose.intel.yaml. On a host whose GPU can change between boots (a VM that fails over to another
# hypervisor), add compose.host-gpu.yaml, which scripts/select-gpu.sh points at the right one at every boot
# (docs/installing.md#the-gpu-at-boot).
# COMPOSE_FILE=compose.yaml:compose.gpu.yaml

# Time zone for logs and schedules (a tz database name).
TZ=Etc/UTC

# The user and group Plex, Tautulli and Kometa run as. They must be able to read and write the media library and
# their own data directories.
PUID=1000
PGID=1000

# The file-creation mask Plex and Tautulli use (optional; 002 when unset).
UMASK=002

# The media library Plex serves and AURA saves artwork into, mounted read-write. scripts/backup.sh never archives
# it, so protect it on the storage that holds it (snapshots).
MEDIA_PATH=/srv/media

# Where every app keeps its data, as host directories: CONFIG_ROOT/<app>/config holds each app's settings and
# database (<app> is the service's name: plex, tautulli, aura, kometa, imagemaid, quickstart), and the app's other
# folders sit beside it: Plex's cache (CONFIG_ROOT/plex/cache, disposable, never backed up) and transcodes in
# progress (CONFIG_ROOT/plex/transcode, never backed up; mount fast local disk there if CONFIG_ROOT isn't on one).
# AURA writes artwork sets for Kometa into CONFIG_ROOT/kometa/config/aura, and Kometa reads AURA's artwork from
# CONFIG_ROOT/aura/config/auraassets. Kometa's .env (its Plex token and API keys, from kometa.env.example) goes in
# CONFIG_ROOT/kometa/config; its config.yml and collection files come from kometa/ in this checkout, mounted
# read-only over the copies there. Create the directories, owned by PUID:PGID, before the first start. The Dozzle
# agent's certificate and key go in CONFIG_ROOT/dozzle/certs, owned by root, the same pair as the Dozzle hub's; not
# backed up (docs/installing.md#dozzles-certificate).
# Never point it into /var/lib/docker/volumes: `docker volume prune` deletes any volume no container mounts as a
# volume, even one whose _data folder a service bind-mounts (docs/installing.md#where-data-lives).
CONFIG_ROOT=/srv/config

# When Kometa runs each day (24-hour HH:MM, comma-separated for several runs). Keep it clear of the nightly backup
# (01:00, scripts/scheduled-backup.sh), which stops Plex and Kometa while it copies their data.
KOMETA_TIMES=07:30

# When ImageMaid runs, in its own schedule syntax (time|frequency, optionally |mode=..., comma-separated for
# several runs). Its other settings (Plex's address and token, the default mode) are in its data directory's .env.
IMAGEMAID_SCHEDULE=22:00|weekly(sunday)
